A||N||3||rodmcneill||Windsheild  washer||||1||
Z||000000||rodmcneill||11-13-2000||11:31 PM||||I have no power going to my windsheild washer motor.I have been using the shop manual and have it down to the wiper pulse module. Where exactly is this located? The shop manual says on outside of RH steering column brkt.I am having a hard time locating this. What does it look like? Thanks guys with the winter coming I really need to get this fixed.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||11-14-2000||08:21 PM||||it's way the heck up under the dash. sort of behind the tach. (position wise I mean. not in the gauge cluster.) I think you'll need the trim under the steering column out to see it.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||11-14-2000||08:32 PM||||Yes, you will have to remove the lower trim piece to get at it.  When laying down in the car, looking at the steering column, I believe it will be to your left, mounted up there somewhere.  It may be hidden by a wiring harness or two.  It looks like a silver heat sink, about 2 inches by 2 inches; if my memory serves me correctly.  Hope this helps!<P>------------------<BR>"The fish who keeps on swimming is the first to chill upstream"||||reg||3
Z||000003||Rodrv6||11-14-2000||09:21 PM||||On mine the wiper pulse module is black.  It will have an electrical plug on both ends.  If you disconnect both plugs and hook them together you can bypass the module.  The wipers and washer should work like a car not equipped with delay wipers. (The washer should spray, but the wiper will not automatically make its 3 sweeps.)<BR>The silver thing with only one connector is the dimming unit for the dash lights.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting :)||||reg||1
